course: dictionary
lesson: 10778
title: Vague: not clear or exact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vague means not clear or exact. When you meet it, read the words around it, because they are the context and they leave clues. «Its border with the next land might be a vague stretch of forest.» The border is not a sharp line. It is a fuzzy patch where you cannot tell exactly where one land ends.
explain: Maths problems often use vague words too. «A few» or «some» do not give an exact number. To check, swap in an exact word and see if the sentence still makes sense. If you can only say «a few» and not «three», the word is vague.
explain: Vague can also describe a shape or a memory that is hard to see or remember clearly. You can vaguely remember a song, which means you only half remember it. A vague person is absent-minded and does not explain things clearly.
explain: Vague is not always bad. «Not every vague answer needs cracking open; sometimes leaving space lets people tell you later.» But when someone asks you for facts, vague words like «and stuff» or «things» do not give the answer, so give the exact details.
fact: Vague means not clear or exact.
fact: Vague words like «and stuff» or «things» do not count as an answer.
fact: Vague is an adjective (vague, vaguer, vaguest), vaguely is an adverb, and vagueness is a noun.
fact: Phrases to know: a vague idea, rather vague, vaguely remember.
fact: A vague shape in the fog is hard to see clearly, and vague words meant to mislead are not honest.
exercise: Your teacher says, «Your answer is too vague.» What does vague mean? | Very long and full of details | Loud and cheerful | *Not clear or exact | Clear and exact
exercise: «For a computer, vague words like "a pinch" or "bake till done" must become exact checks.» Find the word that means the opposite of vague. | checks | *exact | pinch | bake
exercise: Nadia says, «I vaguely remember the song.» What does vaguely mean here? | *Only partly, not clearly | Quickly, without stopping | Word for word, every line | Very loudly and happily
test: Which word in maths is vague because it does not give an exact number? | Twelve | Half | *A few | Seven
test: Your teacher says your answer is too vague. What should you do? | Speak more quietly | Say "a thing" again | *Give the exact details | Say nothing at all
exam: What does «a vague idea» mean? | *An idea that is not yet clear | An idea that is written in gold | An idea that is very big | An idea that everyone already knows
